  "content": {
    "id": "p4-q12-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "12",
    "prompt": "At a gathering of men, women and children, every man shakes hands with every woman for a total of 300 handshakes. Every man shakes hands with every child for a total of 360 handshakes. Every woman shakes hands with every child for a total of 270 handshakes. Determine the total number of people at the gathering.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": {
        "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
        "version": 1,
        "blocks": [
          {
            "id": "p4-q12-short-result",
            "type": "paragraph",
            "fontSize": null,
            "align": "left",
            "spaceBefore": 0,
            "spaceAfter": 2,
            "lineHeight": 1.4,
            "indent": 0,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "53 people.",
                "marks": []
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "p4-q12-short-method",
            "type": "paragraph",
            "fontSize": null,
            "align": "left",
            "spaceBefore": 0,
            "spaceAfter": 2,
            "lineHeight": 1.4,
            "indent": 0,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Use the three products of group sizes to find 20 men, 15 women and 18 children.",
                "marks": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "worked": "Let $m$, $w$ and $c$ be the numbers of men, women and children. By the multiplication principle,\n$$\\begin{align*}mw&=300\\\\mc&=360\\\\wc&=270.\\end{align*}$$\nTherefore,\n$$\\begin{align*}m^2&=\\frac{(mw)(mc)}{wc}\\\\m^2&=\\frac{300\\times360}{270}\\\\m^2&=400\\\\m&=20.\\end{align*}$$\nThe group sizes are positive, so take the positive square root.\n$$\\begin{align*}w&=\\frac{300}{20}\\\\w&=15\\\\c&=\\frac{360}{20}\\\\c&=18\\\\m+w+c&=20+15+18\\\\m+w+c&=53.\\end{align*}$$\nThere are 53 people at the gathering.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 64
  },
